# Build-time configuration for the hosted product at proof.viralhostdigital.com.
#
# Committed on purpose. Every value here is an ADDRESS, never a credential — a VITE_ prefix is a
# promise to compile the value into client code where anyone can read it, so an address is the only
# thing that may go in one. See the long note in .env.example.
#
# This file exists because the relay was previously passed inline at build time and lived nowhere:
#
#     VITE_MODEL_PROXY_BASE=https://... pnpm build
#
# which made the deployed product one forgotten prefix away from silently reverting to the keyless
# lane. It did exactly that on 2026-08-05 — a rebuild dropped the variable, the header went from
# "live models" to "no key", and nothing failed. Vite loads this file automatically for `pnpm build`,
# so the recipe is now `pnpm build` and there is no incantation to remember.

# The public model relay. Holds the OpenRouter key on its own side and attaches it per request; the
# browser sends no Authorization header at all. Terraform: viral-host-digital/model-proxy.tf.
VITE_MODEL_PROXY_BASE=https://hbpv6ohbk8.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/v1
